N2  - Lung cancer is currently the malignant tumor with the highest morbidity and mortality in the world, thoracoscopic segmentectomy is one of the main surgical procedures for the treatment of early stage non-small cell lung cancer (NSCLC). In recent years, three-dimensional computed tomography bronchography and angiography (3D-CTBA) technology has developed rapidly with advantages of stereoscopic presentation of lung anatomy, accurate localization of lung lesions and design of surgical safety margin model, it provides a reliable method for thoracoscopic segmentectomy. This article reviews the current applications of 3D - CTBA in thoracoscopic segmentectomy for stage T1a-1bN0M0 NSCLC.
