N2  - TYPE: Late Breaking Abstract TOPIC: Cardiothoracic Surgery PURPOSE: Compared to Uniportal VATS Lobectomy has Uniportal VATS segmentectomy more potential complications same as air Leckage, Pneumonectomy and postoperative atelectasis. We compared in this study early postoperative outcomes of this two group of patients undergone an anatomical resection between 31.07.2017 until 31.08.2021. METHODS: We compared early outcome of the patients undergone VATS segmentectomy versus the patients undergone VATS Lobectomy in early stage of NSCLC between 01.07.2017 until 31.07.2021. All complications werde registered and reported. Adjustment of patient characteristics was performed using a propensity score. RESULTS: From 85 undergone UVATS segmentectomy was registered and found 21,2% complications ( air Leckage, Pneumonectomy, postoperative bleeding, cardiac arrhythmia, postoperative empyema…) and from 119 patients undergone UVATS Lobectomy was registered 24,9% complications. lung function after 3 month has been shown a better quality of life in patients undergone segmentectomy compared to VATS Lobectomy group. Late postoperative complications ( Pleural effusion, Pneumonectomy and late pleural empyema) was lower in patients undergone VATS segmentectomy. CONCLUSIONS: The rate of complications in VATS segmentectomy group was a little lower than VATs Lobectomy patients. The quality of life in patients undergone VATS segmentectomy was significantly higher than who undergone Lobectomy. CLINICAL IMPLICATIONS: The rate of complications in VATS segmentectomy group was a little lower than VATs Lobectomy patients. The quality of life in patients undergone VATS segmentectomy was significantly higher than who undergone Lobectomy. DISCLOSURE: Nothing to declare.
