N2  - The proceedings contain 65 papers. The topics discussed include: short- and long-term outcomes after total arch replacement by using the trifurcated graft technique, antegrade cerebral perfusion, and deep hypothermia circulatory arrest; A2 the scan, the needle, or the knife? national trends in diagnosing stage I lung cancer; transfusion in elective proximal aortic reconstruction: where do we currently stand?; safety and feasibility of thoracoscopic lung resection for non-small -cell lung cancer in octogenarians; association between centers for disease control 'high-risk' donor characteristics and recipient outcomes after heart transplantation: insights from the UNOS database; trends in surgical approach to thymectomy: an analysis of the national cancer database; sternal wound complications in patients undergoing orthotopic heart transplantation; robotic segmentectomy versus thoracoscopic segmentectomy: comparing intraoperative results; and hospitalizations prior to index admission for ventricular assist device implantation decrease mortality and cost.
