N2  - The proceedings contain 237 papers. The topics discussed include: propensity score-matched analysis of stage I-II non-small cell lung cancer treated by video-assisted thoracoscopic lobectomy or stereotactic ablative radiotherapy; video-assisted thoracoscopic pneumonectomy is safe and may have benefits over open pneumonectomy; uniportal video-assisted thoracoscopic surgery: experience with 471 cases; video-assisted thoracoscopic lobectomy rates before and after adoption of a standardized anterior approach; chemotherapy followed by surgery on the basis of biomarker examination for initially unresectable non-small cell lung cancer patients: a challenging approach; a combined ultrasound of the mediastinum by use of a single ultrasound bronchoscope for non-small cell lung cancer restaging: a prospective study; and may pneumonectomy have a role in the multimodal treatment of locally advanced non-small cell lung cancer?.
