N2  - Objectives: The aim of the work is to evaluate the validity of video-thoracoscopic staging and treatment of non-small cell lung cancer (NSCLC) 20 years after the first thoracoscopic lobectomy. Methods: We retrospectively reviewed 1549 patients, candidates for resection after conventional staging, from November 1991 to December 2010, but submitted to video-thoracoscopy immediately before the procedure. Patients resectable at video-exploration were directly operated on by thoracoscopy or thoracotomy. Only stage I cancer was thoracoscopically removed; others were converted even when thoracoscopically resectable. The impact of preliminary video-thoracoscopy and Kaplan-Meier survival of video-resections were analysed with SPSS software. Results: Video-thoracoscopy disclosed inoperability in 58 (3.7%) out of 1549 patients, mostly for pleural carcinosis (32 patients, 2%) or mediastinal infiltration (22 patients, 1.7%). Five hundred and thirty-four (34.5%) patients had video-thoracoscopic resection (286 lobectomies, 7 pneumonectomies, 241 wedge resections), 923 (59.5%) had thoracotomy resection, and 34 (2.1%) had exploratory thoracotomies (ET). Thoracoscopy was reliable in excluding unresectability (NPV 0.97). Thoracoscopy was more accurate for staging (73.3%) than CT (48.7%) (P<0.0001). Preliminary thoracoscopy decreased ET rate to 2.1% and spared 592 (38.2%) thoracotomies. There was no intraoperative mortality or recurrence among the 286 video-lobectomies. Better five-year survival was found in T1N0 (71.2%) and age under 70 (72.3%) patients than in T2N0 (56.2%) and older patients (37.1%) (P<0.01). Survival after video wedge resection performed in frail patients is significantly better (P=0.016) for smaller than 2 cm tumours (54%) than for larger (32%). Conclusions: Preliminary video-thoracoscopy reliably assesses tumour resectability and feasibility of thoracoscopic resection, limiting unnecessary thoracotomies. Video-lobectomies are safe and survival is comparable to open lobectomy. Video-sublobar resection, in selected cases, is an acceptable option.
